---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 7</p>
  <h1>Advice and obligation with <em>should</em>, <em>must</em>, and <em>have to</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Give advice, talk about rules, and say what is necessary: <span class="ex">You should rest</span>, <span class="ex">I have to renew my visa</span>, <span class="ex">Visitors must sign in</span>, and <span class="ex">You don’t have to pay now.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 55–65 min</span>
    <span class="tag">advice and obligation</span>
    <span class="tag">should · must · have to</span>
    <span class="tag">mustn’t vs don’t have to</span>
    <span class="tag">11 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Watch should, must, and have to on a first day at work.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Find the base verb and the one verb that changes.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose forms, read a clinic message, build questions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give real advice and describe your real rules.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">These three verbs all put pressure on an action. The difference is not only grammar; it is who says so and how strong the pressure is: friendly advice, an outside rule, or a firm prohibition.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Answer from memory, then check. Say each complete sentence aloud.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can">can</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="can’t">can’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Close">Close</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Don’t close">Don’t close</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="works">works</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="work">work</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Marco <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> speak three languages, so he translates for the team. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1: can)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Close" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the door, please. It’s noisy outside. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1: imperatives)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="works" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> at a clinic downtown. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(A1: present simple)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A new job, day one</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Welcome! You have to sign in every morning at the front desk. Everyone must wear an ID badge in the building. You don’t have to work late; we finish at five. And you should ask questions. Really, ask anything."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which sentences state rules, and which one is friendly advice?</li>
      <li>Look at the verbs after <span class="ex">should</span>, <span class="ex">must</span>, and <span class="ex">have to</span>: <span class="ex">sign</span>, <span class="ex">wear</span>, <span class="ex">work</span>, <span class="ex">ask</span>. What form are they in?</li>
      <li>Does <span class="ex">You don’t have to work late</span> prohibit late work, or say it is not necessary?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check: choose the pattern</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">After <b>should</b> and <b>must</b>, look for the base verb. Watch what <b>have to</b> does with the subject.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="leave">leave</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="leaves">leaves</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="to leave">to leave</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="pay">pay</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="pays">pays</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have">have</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has">has</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Do">Do</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>He must <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="leave" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> before six.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>You should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="pay" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> by card. It’s faster.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to catch the early train.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>They <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to catch the early train.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Do" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> you have to work on Saturdays?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Does he <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> to sign the form?</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The system: two families of forms</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">Should</span> and <span class="ex">must</span> are modals: one form for every subject, followed by the base verb. <span class="ex">Have to</span> is different: it conjugates like a normal verb.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th>should / must (modal)</th><th>have to (normal verb)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>positive</b></td><td>She should call back. He must sign here.</td><td>I have to leave at six. She has to leave at six.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>he / she / it</b></td><td>No -s, ever: she should, he must.</td><td>Adds -s: she has to, he has to.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>negative</b></td><td>shouldn’t, mustn’t. No do.</td><td>don’t have to, doesn’t have to.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>question</b></td><td>Should I call? No do.</td><td>Do I have to call? Does she have to call?</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">Important: say <span class="ex">She should call</span>, never <span class="ex">She shoulds call</span> or <span class="ex">Does she should call?</span> Modals refuse -s and refuse do. <span class="ex">Have to</span> is the opposite: it needs <span class="ex">does</span> and <span class="ex">doesn’t</span> like any normal verb.</p>

  <h2>Get to the root: who says so?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>All three verbs press on the same action, but the pressure has a source and a strength. Climb the ladder from a friendly idea to a firm rule.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>verb</th><th>strength</th><th>who says so</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>should</b></td><td>advice, a good idea</td><td>the speaker’s opinion</td><td><span class="contraction">You should back up your files.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>have to</b></td><td>obligation</td><td>outside pressure: laws, schedules, bosses, contracts</td><td><span class="contraction">I have to renew my visa in June.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>must</b></td><td>strong obligation</td><td>the speaker’s own authority, or official rules and signs</td><td><span class="contraction">You must wear a helmet on site.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line">You can ignore <span class="ex">should</span> and stay polite. You cannot ignore <span class="ex">have to</span> or <span class="ex">must</span> without a consequence.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the right pressure</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Think about who says so: the speaker’s advice, an outside rule, or a firm prohibition. Check the subject too.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="should">should</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="shouldn’t">shouldn’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="must">must</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="mustn’t">mustn’t</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="have to">have to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has to">has to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="don’t have to">don’t have to</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="doesn’t have to">doesn’t have to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>You look really tired. You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="should" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> see a doctor. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(advice)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="shouldn’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> answer work email at midnight. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(advice against a habit)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>I <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="have to" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> renew my visa before June. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the law says so)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Ana <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has to" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> start at seven. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(her schedule says so)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Visitors <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="must" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> sign in at the front desk. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(sign at the entrance)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>You <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="mustn’t" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> share this password with anyone. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(prohibited)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>We <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="don’t have to" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> come to the office on Fridays. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(it is optional)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="doesn’t have to" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> wear a suit. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(his office is casual)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The trap: <em>mustn’t</em> and <em>don’t have to</em></h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Same grammar slot, opposite worlds</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"You mustn’t open that email."</span><br /><span class="ex">"You don’t have to open that email."</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>mustn’t</strong> = prohibited. Do not do it. There is a rule against it.</li>
      <li><strong>don’t have to</strong> = not necessary. You can do it or skip it. Your choice.</li>
      <li>Test yourself: which sentence comes from a security warning? Which one comes from a relaxed coworker?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="note-line">The positives feel similar, but the negatives split apart. <span class="ex">Mustn’t</span> closes a door. <span class="ex">Don’t have to</span> opens one.</p>

  <h3>Questions: Should I…? and Do I have to…?</h3>
  <p>Choose the question by what you want to know.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>you want</th><th>ask</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>advice</b></td><td>Should I…?</td><td><span class="contraction">Should I take the earlier train?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>to know the rule</b></td><td>Do I have to…? / Does she have to…?</td><td><span class="contraction">Do I have to pay in advance?</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">Must I…?</span> exists, but it sounds formal and is rare in American English. To ask about a rule, people normally say <span class="ex">Do I have to…?</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2: type the missing word</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Type one word in each gap. <b>Have to</b> builds questions with <b>do</b> and <b>does</b>. Remember: <b>mustn’t</b> prohibits; <b>don’t have to</b> means it is not necessary.</p>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Should" aria-label="answer 1" /> I see a doctor about this cough? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(asking for advice)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Do" aria-label="answer 2" /> we have to pay in advance? &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(asking about the rule)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><input class="answer-input" data-answer="Does" aria-label="answer 3" /> she have to work this weekend?</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>You <input class="answer-input" data-answer="don’t" aria-label="answer 4" /> have to print the ticket. The email is enough.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>You <input class="answer-input" data-answer="mustn’t" aria-label="answer 5" /> smoke in the building. It is prohibited.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Do I have to sign here? Yes, you <input class="answer-input" data-answer="do" aria-label="answer 6" />.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A message from the clinic</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">"Hello Mr. Reyes. Here is your plan for the week after your surgery. You should rest this week and sleep at least eight hours. You mustn’t lift anything heavy for two weeks; that is very important. You don’t have to stay home, but you should keep your walks short. You have to come back on Friday so the nurse can check the stitches. Message me if the pain gets worse."</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You separated the advice, the rules, and the things that are optional.">
    <h3>Drill 3: read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="lifting anything heavy">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What is prohibited for two weeks?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="lifting anything heavy">lifting anything heavy</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="staying home">staying home</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="short walks">short walks</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="staying home is not necessary">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. “You don’t have to stay home” means ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="staying home is not necessary">staying home is not necessary</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="staying home is prohibited">staying home is prohibited</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he must stay home">he must stay home</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="return to the clinic">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What does Mr. Reyes have to do on Friday?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="return to the clinic">return to the clinic</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="stay in bed all day">stay in bed all day</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="take a long walk">take a long walk</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="you should see a doctor">
    <h3>Drill 4: build the advice</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Build the sentence. After should, use the base verb with no to.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="doctor">doctor</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="should">should</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="you">You</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="see">see</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="do i have to sign the form">
    <h3>Drill 5: build the question</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Ask about the rule. Have to needs do at the front.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="sign">sign</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="do">Do</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="form">form</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">the</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="to">to</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="to" data-fix="She must finish the report today." data-why="After must and should, use the base verb without to. Say She must finish, not She must to finish.">
    <h3>Drill 6: after must</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">She</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="must">must</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="finish">finish</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="report">the report today.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="don’t" data-fix="He doesn’t have to work on Fridays." data-why="Have to changes with the subject like a normal verb. With he, she, and it, use doesn’t have to.">
    <h3>Drill 7: have to changes with the subject</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="he">He</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="don’t">don’t</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="have to">have to</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="work">work</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="fridays">on Fridays.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8: say it, then reveal</h3>
    <p>Read the cue, say the full sentence aloud, then reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> I should call the bank. Change to he.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He should call the bank.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> She has to work tonight. Make a yes / no question.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Does she have to work tonight?</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> You have to wear a tie. Make it negative: the tie is optional.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You don’t have to wear a tie.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Parking here is prohibited. Say the rule with mustn’t.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You mustn’t park here.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> He has to travel for work. Make it negative.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He doesn’t have to travel for work.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>6</b> We have to be there at nine. Change to she.</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She has to be there at nine.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Advice corner:</b> Your teacher says: “I can’t sleep at night.” Give three pieces of advice with <span class="ex">should</span> or <span class="ex">shouldn’t</span>. <span class="ex">You should stop drinking coffee after lunch.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your real rules:</b> Say three things you have to do for work or study, and one thing you don’t have to do. <span class="ex">I have to answer emails every day. I don’t have to go to the office on Fridays.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Signs in your city:</b> Think of two real signs near your home. Say the rules with <span class="ex">must</span> or <span class="ex">mustn’t</span>. <span class="ex">You mustn’t park on this street. Drivers must stop for the tram.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask the teacher:</b> Ask two <span class="ex">Do you have to…?</span> questions about the teacher’s job, then one <span class="ex">Should I…?</span> question about your English. <span class="ex">Do you have to plan every lesson? Should I read more in English?</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Same and different:</b> Compare your rules with a friend’s or a family member’s. <span class="ex">I have to start at eight, but she doesn’t have to start until ten.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “After should and must, I use the ______ verb for every subject. Have to changes with the subject: he ______ to. Mustn’t means it is ______. Don’t have to means it is not ______.”</p>
    <p>Then give one piece of real advice, say one real rule from your life, and name one thing you don’t have to do tomorrow.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can give advice with should, state rules with must and have to, and keep mustn’t and don’t have to apart.">
    <h3>Final quiz: advice, obligation, and the negatives</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="doesn’t have to">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. She ___ come to the meeting. It is optional.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="doesn’t have to">doesn’t have to</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="mustn’t">mustn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="must">must</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="mustn’t">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. The sign says “No smoking.” You ___ smoke here.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="mustn’t">mustn’t</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="don’t have to">don’t have to</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="shouldn’t">shouldn’t</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="drink">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. He should ___ more water.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="drink">drink</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="drinks">drinks</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="to drink">to drink</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Do">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. ___ I have to book a seat in advance?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do">Do</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Should">Should</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Must">Must</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="has">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. Ana ___ to renew her passport. It expires next month.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="has">has</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="have">have</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="must">must</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="You should take the earlier train.">
        <p class="quiz-question">6. Which sentence gives advice?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="You should take the earlier train.">You should take the earlier train.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Visitors must sign in at the desk.">Visitors must sign in at the desk.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="I have to renew my visa.">I have to renew my visa.</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="paying now is not necessary">
        <p class="quiz-question">7. “You don’t have to pay now” means ___.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="paying now is not necessary">paying now is not necessary</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="paying now is prohibited">paying now is prohibited</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="you should never pay">you should never pay</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Do I have to check in online?">
        <p class="quiz-question">8. Which question asks about a rule?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Do I have to check in online?">Do I have to check in online?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Should I check in online?">Should I check in online?</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Have I to check in online?">Have I to check in online?</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
